  "notes": "Quarter-by-quarter Program of Study from Appendix A of Galen's official 'Application for Intent to Open a Physical Building and Establish a Nursing Education Program: Associate Degree in Nursing Program' submitted to the Utah Board of Nursing (October 24, 2022; updated February 22, 2023) for the Salt Lake Campus, 344 West 13800 South, Draper, UT 84020. The filing states the ADN 'is currently offered at other Galen campuses, has an existing faculty-developed curriculum' and will be supervised by the Main Campus in Louisville, KY. Galen runs on a QUARTER calendar; seeded as published in quarters. Sequenced sum = 79 quarter credits; the filing additionally awards 20 quarter credits 'Credit for PN/VN Licensure' (NOT sequenced), for a total degree requirement of 99 quarter credits. Admission requires proof of active, unencumbered PN/VN licensure and diploma (per Galen's admissions requirements). Downstream semester-gated checks (associate 4-7 / bachelor 8-12 semester gates) are semester-calibrated and do not apply to quarter terms without conversion. No course-level prerequisites are listed in the plan of study tables.",
